Z||000018||deceler8||09-18-2001||01:26 PM||||Be patient. I've heard the Taliban is supposedly massing troops and equipment at the Pakistan border. Great. The road back to Kabul will look like the Highway of Death in Iraq.<P>This nation has not been ignoring the threat like many claim. One of the things we have going for us is that most of the Middle Eastern nations want no part of bin Laden, or Arafat, for that matter. Most of the states bordering Afghanistan have closed their borders not to prevent a bin Laden escape, but rather to keep out refugees. So these states want nothing to do with these people either. Most Afghans do not want bin Laden around either. <P>And the general thought that these people do not fear death is just not borne out by the numbers. If they didn't fear death, why have 2 million Afghans fled to Iran and Pakistan in the past year ? If they ain't afraid of death, why are they running ?<P>||||reg||1
